\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty surges further ahead. \b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The zloty forged ahead again on Tuesday with no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its relentless rise, and traders saw it edging even higher. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed slightly as the yen inched back under 145 to the dollar, with the rupiah gaining sharply on support from Indonesia's latest round of international aid. \par \par \uc2  In Warsaw, the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through the barrier of nine percent above parity for the first time, closing at a new record of 9.08/9.03 percent above parity compared with Monday's record high close of 8.89/8.84. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't look like any respite for the strong zloty," said one trader at a London bank, who asked not to be named. \par \par \uc2  By 1245 GMT the Polish unit was at 3.432 bid against the dollar in London and 1.9246 against the mark, the two main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the five-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket which determines the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily parity rate, compared with 3.436 and 1.9255 respectively in late London trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The zloty is allowed to fluctuate in a band of plus or minus 10 percent around the parity rate. Last week the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to cap the rise, but there was no confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Tuesday in spite of earlier expectations that it would again buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Usually the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend a level for a couple of days and then allow the market to take it through. They're basically slowing the rise," the trader said, adding that he saw the next resistance level at 9.25 percent or even 9.5 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and traders said demand for zlotys was bolstered by privatisation issues and foreign purchases of Polish bonds. \par \par \uc2  Most East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed slightly as the yen backtracked to below 145 to the dollar after earlier crashing through 146. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen is providing the general framework for movements in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Andrew Fung, an economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are higher on the back of the slightly firmer yen, although what we've seen in European time is some of these gains being given up." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah saw the biggest gain, climbing back under the 13,000 barrier to 12,800 to the dollar by 1245 GMT, a rise of around 2.7 percent from late Monday's levels in London. \par \par \uc2  Fung said the biggest impetus came from large inflows of aid aimed at dragging Indonesia out of its financial crisis. He said these far outweighed debt service outflows, especially since much of Indonesia's debt servicing was at a standstill. \par \par \uc2  International donors last week pledged $7.9 billion in aid for the current fiscal year to end-March. The IMF has already said it will top up a $41.2 billion international rescue package already in place with a further $6.2 billion in fresh loans. \par \par \uc2  The official launch on Monday of the Indonesian Debt Restructuring Agency (INDRA) was not having much immediate impact on the market, although INDRA's base exchange rate of 13,233 rupiah to the dollar for debt conversion could lend support in the medium term, Fung added. INDRA was born out of a deal struck in June with foreign creditors to restructure the country's $84 billion in private-sector foreign debt. But no companies have yet signed up for the scheme, and Fung said many debtor firms had already acted to restructure their debt. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we'll see any big move across the board to transfer to INDRA," he said. "But there's a psychological cap at 13,233, and in that sense the market will probably stay away from that (level) unless there's a really serious deterioration on the political front." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in emerging markets, the rouble held rock steady at 6.283 bid, unchanged from late Monday's levels in London. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown lost a little of its recent strength amid jitters over the health of President Vaclav Havel, who was seriously ill in hospital, but analysts and traders said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain buoyant. \par \par \uc2  The crown eased to 17.367 bid against the mark, compared with 17.226 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8400xs2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
