\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty hits new high as c.bank stays its hand. \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 15:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The zloty slowly firmed to close at a new record high against its basket on Monday with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refraining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said continued foreign interest in Polish treasuries pulled the zloty up to close at 8.89/8.84 percent above the parity rate, from Friday's 8.80/8.76 percent finish. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 3.4390/05 to the dollar, against 3.4335/60 on Friday and at 1.9255/65 to the mark, against 1.9300/30. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty gradually gained ground to close around 8.9 percent. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably wants to keep the market guessing somewhat and so it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," said Mateusz Bieniek, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Over the last few weeks the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sustained gains above 8.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the zloty's appreciation rather than to knock it down. If they wanted to weaken it, they would have to spend much larger sums of money," Bieniek added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday if the zloty kept trading at these levels. \par \par \uc2  They said foreign investors did not buy large amounts of T-bills at Monday's 700 million zloty tender, but that some sought the benchmark 52-week bill. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark's average yield fell 16.18 percent at the tender, in line with expectations, from last week's 16.65. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the economy ministry's forecast of 6.7 percent GDP growth in the first half of 1998 had little impact on the market even though it was better than expected. \par \par \uc2  "This number seems a bit high. It may be better to wait for official second quarter GDP data from the statistical office," said one senior banking analyst in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect Poland's economy, which grew 6.9 percent last year, to slow from the second quarter under the weight of a tight monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The government expects GDP growth of 5.6 percent this year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about six percent. ((Wojciech Moskwa, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du8300vz3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
