\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty stays at all-time high, c.bank quiet. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 31 (Reuters) - The zloty held at an all-time high early on Friday and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in with dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT the zloty was at 8.89/8.86 percent firmer than the trading band centre against the opening 8.89/8.84 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4310/25 to the dollar against 3.4300/15 at the start and at 1.9281/86 to the mark against 1.9290/00. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty is presently at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels and around these levels few players want to buy the unit," said Piotr Konarski, senior dealer at WestLB Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the National Bank of Poland bought an estimated $80 million to cool the foreign-charged zloty, but dealers said the move failed to weaken the market's pro-zloty sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see any reson why the zloty should weaken now and in fact the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  instantly trigger more dollar-selling," WestLB's Konarski added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty moves within a range of 10 percent above or below a parity rate set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Zloty parity is determined by the value of a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the unit is devalued at a rate of 0.65 percent per month. \par \par \uc2  The local money market calmed down on the first day of the new monthly reserve period and overnight and tomorrow/next rates held flat at 19.0/19.4 percent in early Friday trade. ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du7v031kb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
