\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Higher On Optimism Toward Emerging Mkts \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty (PLN) is slightly higher against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Monday morning in quiet dealing amid improved optimism toward emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty is 8.4% above the mid-point against its basket of five key hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from around 8.35% at the close of trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is consolidating after profit-taking on the zloty late last week," said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  However, he estimated the zloty could rise to about 8.5% above the mid-point of its trading band because the zloty remains attractive to foreign investors and because general sentiment to emerging markets is improving. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was at PLN3.4450, down from Friday's fixing of PLN3.4495. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9325, unchanged from Friday's fixing of PLN1.9325. \par \par \uc2  Malgorzata Sawicka, a dealer at Bank Handlowy, said many investors aren't yet active in the market Monday morning because they are looking for new direction to where the zloty might go. \par \par \uc2  The zloty charged to record levels early last week but fell prey to profit-taking by the end of the week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said if the zloty rises to about 8.5% above the midpoint of the trading band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.7591 and for the mark at PLN2.1115. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is 8.35% below its parity rate, and the mark is 8.45% below parity. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.65% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates are between 22.90% and 23.40%. \par \par \uc2  -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0854GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7r06dtw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
