\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rouble slips on rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Casciato \par \uc2 1,105 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1998\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 24 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble continued its recent weakening trend, spurred on by a cut in the nation's benchmark interest rate on Friday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Negative sentiment, already weighing on the rouble, deepened after Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the refinancing rate to 60 percent from 80 percent, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The drop (in the rouble) is probably related, but it was falling already so the rating cut doesn't help," said Juliet Sampson, emerging markets economist at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  The rouble has been pulled down by weak Lower-Developed-Countries (LDC) debt and an overall negative sentiment across markets in general, she said. \par \par \uc2  "It's being pulled down by the yen, by the Dow (Jones industrial average), it's taking any excuse," she said. \par \par \uc2  Sampson said market players remained concerned despite the International Monetary Fund's approval on Monday of an $11.2 billion loan bailout for Russia. \par \par \uc2  "There was a lot of enthusiasm when the deal went through and now people are doing their numbers and saying maybe there are still doubts about whether Russia can make it," she said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Vice President Al Gore said on Friday he was optimistic Russia will turn the corner soon and economic growth will soon appear. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Eastern Europe, the Polish zloty softened in early Friday trade as players continued to take profits on Polish treasuries after recent foreign capital inflows pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to all-time highs and yields to lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 1110 GMT the zloty was 8.25 percent firmer than the trading band centre against the opening 8.35/8.29 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4525/40 to the dollar against 3.4500/20 at the start and at 1.9355/60 to the mark against 1.9320/35. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the overall positive sentiment toward Poland remained intact, adding that the zloty should continue to find support above 8.0 percent from the trading band centre. \par \par \uc2  "We are still seeing some profit-taking, but there are also investors who are selling larger amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the zloty weakens to around 8.15-8.20 percent from parity," said Piotr Konarski, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at WestLB Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty on Thursday after buying roughly $180 million on the market earlier this week to cool the surging zloty. \par \par \uc2  Poland's zloty moves within a range of 10 percent above or below a parity rate set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Zloty parity is determined by the value of a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the unit is devalued at a rate of 0.65 percent per month. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown also slipped on sagging emerging markets sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Newly elected Czech Prime Minister Milos Zeman said on Friday his government would like to participate in the setting of inflation targets along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the election of Foreign Minister Keizo Obuchi as the new leader of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party had a muted effect. \par \par \uc2  Obuchi's win had been largely factored into the market and players have begun to focus on the make-up of his new cabinet. \par \par \uc2  Even the Malaysian ringgit shrugged off a ratings downgrade from Moody's Investors Service. The U.S.-based ratings agency said it downgraded Malaysia's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceilings for bonds and notes to Baa2 from A2. \par \par \uc2  "The downgradings were not particularly surprising and were expected somewhat," said Mitul Kotecha, emerging markets economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit rose to 4.1250/1450 from 4.1430/630 in late European trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Buying interest in Malaysian assets from foreign companies had underpinned the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kotecha said. \par \par \uc2  "There are reports of investments taking place in Malaysian assets from foreign companies and that is probably helping keep up the ringgit at least for today." \par \par \uc2  Moody's said it cut the country ceiling for bank deposits to Baa3 from Baa1, lowered the short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  country ceilings for debt and bank deposits to Prime 3 from Prime 2 and cut foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds of the government to Baa2 from A2. \par \par \uc2  Moody's said the ratings action reflected the rapid deterioration in Malaysia's economy this year and the expected effects on the banking system and government finance. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah slipped below the 14,000 per dollar level, with the market focused on next week's meeting of Indonesia's donors in Paris. \par \par \uc2  Planning Minister Boediono said the group was likely to pledge a larger amount of loans than last year's $5.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  IMF Asia expert Hubert Neiss said the timing for scrapping food subsidies in Indonesia depended on the economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia on Thursday approved an adjusted 1998/99 budget of 236.89 trillion rupiah, from the previous 277.14 trillion to reflect a drop in repayment of foreign debt principal. \par \par \uc2  But the country's economic and social woes looked set to persist with national airline Garuda Indonesia saying it expected a net loss of two trillion rupiah in calendar 1998. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT. \par \par \uc2  The following is a snapshot of emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  * ASIA \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Indonesian rupiah\tab 13,900 per dollar bid vs 14,000 late in\par \tab \tab \tab \tab  London on Thursday.\par * Malaysian ringgit\tab 4.12 per dollar bid vs 4.143\par * Thai baht\tab \tab   at 40.80 per dollar vs 41.25\par * Philippine peso\tab   41.9 per dollar vs 42\par * South Korean won\tab  at 1,244 per dollar vs 1,273\par * Singapore dollar\tab  1.7105 per dollar versus 1.7105\par * Indian rupee\tab      42.49 per dollar vs 42.45.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * EUROPE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Russian rouble\tab    at 6.270 per dollar bid vs 62600 on Thursday.\par * Zloty\tab \tab \tab 8.25 percent above target basket parity vs 8.53 \tab \tab \tab \tab  percent on Thursday.\par * Mark/Czech crown\tab  at 17.669 bid vs 17.540\par * Slovak crown\tab      19.411 on mark vs 19.360\par * Hungarian forint\tab  121.31 vs mark against 120.98\par * Ukrainian hryvnia\tab at 2.1290 per dollar vs 2.12\par * Romanian leu\tab      at 8,720 per dollar vs 8,705\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * AFRICA & MIDEAST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Israeli shekel\tab    3.6639 bid on dollar from Thursday's 3.6699\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * South African rand     at 6.1750 per dollar vs 6.2200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Kenyan shilling\tab   at 59.10 vs 59.05\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * LATIN AMERICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mexican peso\tab      at 8.85 per dollar vs 8.863\par * Brazil's real\tab     at 1.165 per dollar vs 1.164\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London newsroom +44 171 542 6762, fax 583 7239,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7o0065t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
