\par\par \b \uc2  Profit-taking pushes zloty lower in early trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1998\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 24 (Reuters) - The zloty softened in early Friday trade as players continued to take profits on Polish treasuries after recent foreign capital inflows pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to all-time highs and yields to lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0835 GMT the zloty was at 8.25/8.18 percent firmer than the trading band centre against the opening 8.35/8.29 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4530/50 to the dollar against 3.4500/20 at the start and at 1.9346/66 to the marlk against 1.9320/35. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the overall positive sentiment towards Poland remained intact, adding that the zloty should find support on Friday above 8.0 percent from the trading band centre. \par \par \uc2  "We are still seeing some profit-taking, but there are also investors who are selling larger amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the zloty weakens to around 8.15-8.20 percent from parity," said Piotr Konarski, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at WestLB Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty on Thursday after buying roughly $180 million on the market earlier this week to cool the surging zloty. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 52-week T-bill traded at 16.60/16.35 percent early on Friday against Thursday's 16.45/16.20 percent and this week's low of less than 16.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Poland's zloty moves within a range of 10 percent above or below a parity rate set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Zloty parity is determined by the value of a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the unit is devalued at a rate of 0.65 percent per month. \par \par \uc2  Polish short-term rates edged lower on Friday as banks had cash surpluses after tax payment period was over. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight rates were at 19.80/20.20 percent against the opening 20.00/21.00 percent. Tomorrow/next rates traded at 19.65/20.55 percent against 20.00/21.00 percent at the start. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7o005fd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
