\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty rides to new high despite c. bank action. \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1998\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty for the second day to cool positive sentiment for the Polish unit but could not stop it closing at a fresh all-time high on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 8.79/8.76 percent above the trading band centre, a touch higher than Tuesday's record close of 8.77/8.74 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland (NBP) bought an estimated $60-80 million on Wednesday when the zloty was between 8.80 and 8.75 percent, after buying roughly $100 million in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign investors mainly stayed on the sidelines today, waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before making any deals. Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were just intended to show the NBP is watching, not to weaken the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank in Warsaw said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 3.4374/84 per dollar, against 3.4340/55 on Tuesday and at 1.9214/20 to the mark, against 1.9210/15. \par \par \uc2  "Most players are long on the zloty, waiting for NBP moves, but others feel that this is the top and the zloty could slowly drift down towards 8.5 percent," said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that in the longer-term Poland's still high yields and relatively sound fundementals would attract more foreign portfolio capital and keep the zloty buoyant. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 52-week T-bill yield fell some 0.3 point during Wednesday's session, ending around 16.00/15.80 percent against Monday's primary auction yield of 16.69 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said markets received a small boost from NBP chief Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz's comment that the level of speculative foreign capital in Poland's treasuries was at a safe level. \par \par \uc2  "We are not under presssure from speculative capital," Gronkiewicz-Watlz told the Wprost weekly in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "If it (speculative capital) topped 20 percent we could be worried, but it...never did. Not too long ago we had some 13 to 14 percent held by speculators," Gronkiewicz-Waltz said. \par \par \uc2  Poland's zloty moves within a range of 10 percent above or below a parity rate set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Zloty parity is determined by the value of a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the unit is devalued at a rate of 0.65 percent per month. \par \par \uc2  ((Wojciech Moskwa, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7m00h40\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
