\par\par \b \uc2  Polish RPP member says  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\uc2  needed. \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 22 (Reuters) - A member of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (RPP) said \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were needed to cool demand for the surging zloty, but that the situation was under control, the Gazeta Wyborcza daily reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "So far everything is under control, and what is happening is no surprise to us," Gazeta quoted Grzegorz Wojtowicz as saying. \par \par \uc2  "I am not able to say how long this situation will last. I think that after some time, investor interest in the zloty will decline. But now \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are necessary to cool investor appetite for the zloty," Wojtowicz said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the zloty, buoyant on foreign buying of Polish treasuries, rose to all time highs of around 8.9 percent above the trading band centre before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. It closed at 8.77 percent. \par \par \uc2  Poland's zloty moves against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a range of 10 percent above or below a parity rate set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-member RPP council last week cut interest rates and reduced the zloty's official devaluation rate. \par \par \uc2  "The council made a correct decision about cutting interest rates, further cuts were not possible," Wojtowicz said. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.c