\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Rises In Early Trading;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1998\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened higher and strengthened slowly against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in thin early dealing Wednesday as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to hang over the market. \par \par \uc2  The zloty opened 8.85% stronger than parity then rose slightly to about 8.87%. This compared with 8.78% at Tuesday's fixing, dealers reported. \par \par \uc2  Around 0818 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4310 zlotys (PLN), down from PLN3.4320 the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of PLN3.4330. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9219, down from PLN1.9229 at the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of PLN1.9220. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at Bank Handlowy said that London banks were offering to sell dollars for zlotys but failing to find takers. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody wants to be stuck with a long zloty position when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for zlotys on Tuesday when the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested the level of 9% above the mid-point of the band, or one percentage point from the band's edge. \par \par \uc2  "If the zloty reaches 9%, the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will enter," said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  Members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council were quoted in Gazeta Wyborcza Wednesday as saying they weren't surprised by the strength of the zloty, given the loan agreement reached between Russia and the International Monetary Fund this week. \par \par \uc2  Council member Grzegorz Wojtowicz said he expected the upward pressure on the zloty to abate eventually. In the meantime, he said, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.7661 and for the mark at PLN2.1082. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 8.90% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 8.84% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.65% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates firmed slightly in early dealing to between 21.50% and 22.50% from between 21.20% and 21.50% at the opening. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0837GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7m066xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
