\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Hits Record Vs Basket;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1998\par 10:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was at record levels against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in nervous dealing early Tuesday as dealers await \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The zloty opened at around 9% stronger than the midpoint of the trading band but then weakened slightly and settled at around 8.8%, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the level of 8.5% on the strong side of the band to keep the zloty from coming too close to the 10% limit. But on Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the zloty to break the 8.5% barrier for the first time. \par \par \uc2  As a result, "The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any moment," said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  Malgorzata Sawicka, a dealer at Bank Handlowy, said that the level of 9% may now be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trip-wire. "If we cross 9%, then certainly there will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was gaining on news of continued progress toward an international aid package for Russia. On Monday, the International Monetary Fund gave approval for a $11.2 billion package including an immediate $4.8 billion outlay. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been buying Polish Treasury bills and bonds, despite last week's cut in key interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 0744 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4260 zlotys (PLN), down from Monday's fixing of PLN3.4320. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9221, down from Monday's fixing of PLN1.9265. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.7603 and for the mark at PLN2.1086. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 8.89% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 8.84% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par is devalued at a rate of 0.65% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate\par within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate.\par -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0806GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7l06575\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
