\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty dips on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1998\par 11:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 14 (Reuters) - The zloty softened early on Tuesday after the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market for the first time in more than two months, knocking the foreign-charged unit from record highs. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the zloty was at 8.44/8.38 percent firmer than the trading band centre against the opening 8.63/8.57 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4520/40 to the dollar against 3.4450/70 at the start and at 1.9195/10 to the mark against 1.9155/70. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers estimates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought at least $40 million on the interbank market on Tuesday when the zloty traded between 8.63 and 8.35 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "Positive sentiment remains intact despite \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we are still seeing dollar-selling both by domestic and foreign investors, said Wojciech Trzepizur, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at bank BRE SA in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  The zloty was lifted to all-time highs late on Monday after news that international lenders had reached agreement with Russia to provide extra loans of $22.6 bln in 1998 and 1999. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty should trade above the 8.0 percent level from parity as a prospect of a near term cut in interest rates and a slowing of the unit's devalution pace, possibly this Thursday, attracts foreign capital to Polish debt. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision-making body, Monetary Policy Council (RPP), is scheduled to meet on Thursday, but it has not been known yet whether it will hold a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are buying Polish paper, expecting rate cuts on Thursday, but a large impulse also came from Russia after its rescue package was secured," said Jaroslaw Dryjski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  Previously the zloty hit an all-time high of around 8.4 percent stronger than the parity rate on May 11, which also prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7e00vgo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
