\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 -Indian rupee weathers storm. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Valerie Darroch \par \uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1998\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee held steady in European trading on Tuesday despite a storm of international protest over India's nuclear tests but London analysts warned of possible weakness ahead. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupee was trading around 39.760/770 in light volume, faring better than in Bombay where the six month forward rate against the dollar jumped to a premium of 8.45 percent versus 6.8 percent at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (rupee) is not one that you can trade actively and the Reserve Bank of India are pretty effective at smoothing things in terms of crisis, so we are unlikely to see a plunge. It's much more likely to happen gently," said Nick Douch, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BZW. \par \par \uc2  The nuclear tests carried out on Monday by India's new coalition government, headed by the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP), have sparked widespread international condemnation and raised the spectre of sanctions being imposed. \par \par \uc2  Both the United States and Japan have said they are considering sanctions. Japan, which is India's largest foreign aid donor, warned on Tuesday that it may freeze loans to India. \par \par \uc2  "We will have to see wait and see what the world reaction is. It's a non-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  story in terms of movement but it's obviously a story that is going to hang around in terms of potential movement," BZW's Douch said. \par \par \uc2  Among other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indonesian rupiah suffered another bout of weakness amid deepening worries over social unrest and a lack of progress on debt restructuring talks. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was little changed after surging in Asian trading on expectations of a landslide victory for Presidential election candidate Joseph Estrada. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht turned slightly weaker, bucking the firmer trend in Bangkok where corporate selling of the dollar supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Among European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Polish zloty was slightly weaker but the easing was expected to be short-lived as foreign capital inflows show no sign of abating. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's persistent rise sparked a bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen it down on Monday and traders said further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely. \par \par \uc2  "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  there is a lot of speculation about a possible cut in the crawling peg and there is also speculation about a cut in interest rates," said Jesper Dannesboe, economist at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  He said that on the one hand the market knows that the monetary policy committee is focusing on putting downward pressure on inflation to hit its 9-1/2 percent target but on the other hand the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is worried about the current account deficit and strong capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  "It's not clear if they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will cut interest rates yet and the bottom line is that the zloty will stay strong for now because the market gets very high yields and it's hard to see them cutting extremely aggressively in the near term," Dannesboe said. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown was also slightly weaker but holding at the key support level of 18.252 after inflation data met market expectations. \par \par \uc2  Dannesboe said fundamentals in the Czech republic were far less strong than in Poland. \par \par \uc2  "Nevertheless the Czech crown is very strong so I would be a bit wary about going long the Czech at these levels. We also have the election at the end of June," he said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5c05hk6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
