\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Up In Early Trade After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1998\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty (PLN)  is sharply higher against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket early Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made no decision at Thursday's Monetary Policy Council meeting. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was 8.3% above the mid-point against its basket of five key hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from around 7.7% at the close of trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'There was a little panic before the meeting,' said Mariusz Dodek, dealer at Societe Generale. But since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came to no real decisions, investors have started buying again, he added. \par \par \uc2  In a statement after the meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said only that the Monetary Policy Council had discussed 'the current monetary situation.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT, the dollar was at PLN3.3695, down from Thursday's fixing of PLN3.3810. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9060, down from Thursday's fixing of PLN1.9185. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the zloty to remain strong but warned that the zloty could become prey to profit-taking later in the session. \par \par \uc2  Malgorzata Sawicka, dealer at Bank Handlowy, also noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty keeps climbing. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6719 and for the mark at PLN2.0775. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is 8.2% below its parity rate, while the mark is 8.3% below parity. \par \par \uc2  The zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.8% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates are between 22.80% and 23.20%. \par \par \uc2  -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0854GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5803vam\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
