\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty weakens as investors take profits. \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 7 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty fell in early Thursday trade as players rebuilt dollar positions on worries of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the outcome of a Monetary Policy Council (RPP) meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters the decision-making RPP was convening early on Thursday, but was unlikely to hold a news conference after its meeting. \par \par \uc2  At 0945 GMT the zloty was at 8.00/7.95 percent firmer than the trading band centre against the opening 8.14/8.02 percent and Wednesday's close at 8.26/8.23 \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.3775/90 to the dollar against 3.3710/50 at the start and at 1.9070/85 to the mark against 1.9060/80. \par \par \uc2  "We had some speculative dollar-buying just at the start of the session as some rebuilt dollar-positions cut ahead of the weekend," said Piotr Konarski, dealer at WestLB Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  "There were also rumours that the RPP is meeting today and the market is very nervous, but I think the zloty should find a strong support around 8.0 percent from parity," Konarski said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday and Wednesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty after the unit hit an intraday all-time high around 8.4 percent. At the last two sessions the bank bought an estimated $140 million on the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed the zloty's fall to an unfavourable mood on Asian emerging markets, which prompted some investors to take profits on the zloty's recent gains. \par \par \uc2  "The local market is nervous and if anything goes wrong on other emerging markets it has some psycholoical effect over here as well," said Rafal Petsch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank of America Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  "Also the NBP's actions show that they are not happy with the zloty's appreciation," Petsch added. \par \par \uc2  Turmoil in Indonesia and a threat of devaluation of the Chinese yuan spooked Asian markets on Thursday, sparking a general slide in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and share prices in the region. \par \par \uc2  Polish short-term cash was stable on Thursday amid balanced trade. Overnight rates were at 23.05/23.25 percent against the opening 23.00/23.35. Tomorrow/next traded at 23.10/23.30 against 23.00/23.35 at the start. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5705wur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
