\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys -2: Also Buys At PLN3.3610 \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 1998\par 13:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to stem the rise of the zloty (PLN), buying dollars for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the PLN3.3605 level, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $10 million when the zloty was at about 8.6% on the strong side of its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at another major bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also bought $10 million at the level of PLN3.3610. \par \par \uc2  Around 1050 GMT, the dollar was quoted at PLN3.3670, down from Monday's fixing of 3.3840. The Deutsche mark was quoted at PLN1.9000, up from Monday's fixing of PLN1.8950. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday morning, the National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6780 and for the mark at PLN2.0639. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at 8.46% below the parity rate, while the mark was quoted at 7.94% below the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  -by Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1108GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5503q55\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
