\par\par \b \uc2  Polish RPP hopes rate cut to slow zloty rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 22 (Reuters) - Poland's Monetary Policy Council (RPP) hopes its Wednesday cut in the main money market rate will ease upward pressure on the zloty and limit the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a RPP member said. \par \par \uc2  The RPP cut its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by one point to 23 percent on Wednesday, while leaving Poland's main interest rates unchanged at 27 and 24.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, a cut in interest rates will as usual cause the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken...this is the direction of our activities in view of what is happening on the market," Grzegorz Wojtowicz told Reuters after the council's meeting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to continue to stage \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the zloty from rising, Wojtowicz said: "I hope for more peace after this rate cut." \par \par \uc2  Large foreign inflows into Polish high-yielding treasuries pushed the zloty up by more than six percentage points since the start of the year and sparked repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-and mark-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Wojtowicz said he hoped that if \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic situation developed well, the Wednesday decision to cut the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate could be the starting point of a longer process of declining interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "I hope so (it is a beginning of some longer process). It's hard to imagine a country having such high real interest rates," Wojtowicz said. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4m06zxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
