\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Gains Vs Basket;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1998\par 10:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty gained against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Monday as foreign investors continued to buy Polish debt securities. \par \par \uc2  With the zloty hovering around 7.75% above the midpoint of the trading band, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0821 GMT, the dollar was at 3.3993 zlotys (PLN), down slightly from PLN3.3995 at the opening but up from Friday's fixing of PLN3.3975. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.8754, down from Friday's fixing of PLN1.8815. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Polish banks are building up zloty positions in anticipation of foreign demand for Polish Treasury bills to be auctioned Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  'Nobody wants to buy dollars,' said Michal Kowalczyk, a dealer at Bank Handlowy. \par \par \uc2  The zloty also gained on comments last week by Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz, president of the National Bank of Poland, that interest rates may be cut this year. The comments were reported in the newspaper Gazeta Wyborcza. \par \par \uc2  Anticipating an interest-rate cut, foreign investors are buying debt securities to lock in current high yields, said Andrzej Rzysko, Treasurer at Societe Generale's Warsaw Branch. \par \par \uc2  'The positive pressure is very strong on the zloty,' Rzysko said, adding that '8% is the next psychological level that will be tested.' \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6797 and for the mark at PLN2.0368. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 7.62% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 7.92% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.8% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 24.00% and 24.20%. \par \par \uc2  -Christopher Wellisz, 48-22-622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0842GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4k039wi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
