\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's reforms set stage for lower rates - finmin. \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 20 (Reuters) - Poland's Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz said on Monday policies to reduce the budget deficit would set the stage for lower interest rates, but declined comment on whether the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should cut rates at this week's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  "I am trying to create a scope, by reducing the budget deficit, for at some stage some response for the lowering of interest rates," Balcerowicz told Reuters Television here. \par \par \uc2  The government's efforts to reduce public spending and accelerate privatization were critical to dealing with heavy foreign capital inflows coming into Poland, he said. \par \par \uc2  But the finance minister said he did not want to influence the monetary policy of Poland's independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The monetary council of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet the day after tomorrow, I wouldn't like to preempt their decision," Balcerowicz said. \par \par \uc2  Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz reiterated over the weekend that a cut in interest rates was possible this year if the economy developed well. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty soared to record highs on Monday amid strong foreign interest in Polish treasury paper, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close at 7.89/7.85 percent above the trading band center, against Friday's 7.60/7.57 percent. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the zloty's rise on Monday. Last week it spent an estimated $130 million. \par \par \uc2  Warsaw analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council may have to take decisions to cool the market's strong pro-zloty sentiment, even though the the Council was not expected to lower rates until the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would widen the zloty's 20-percent trading band or could stop announcing the daily parity rate to create more uncertainty for speculators. \par \par \uc2  (( George Lerner, Emerging Markets Unit, 212-859-1671)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4k072dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
