\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Seen Aiming For 7.5% Level \b0\par\par\uc2 179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par 14:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for zlotys (PLN) at PLN3.3940 late Friday, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer, at a major Western bank here, said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $10 million. \par \par \uc2  Around 1205 GMT, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at PLN3.3975, down from Thursday's fixing of PLN3.4050. The Deutsche mark was quoted at PLN1.8827, up from Thursday's fixing of PLN1.8795. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came when the zloty moved to 7.65% above the midpoint of the trading band. 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to push the zloty down to 7.5% at the fixing,' said a dealer at another bank. 'But I don't think they will succeed,' she added. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.8% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1227GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4h0399x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
