\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty stable but seen testing upside. \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 16 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty held stable in early Thursday trade and dealers said it would again test higher ground amid bullish sentiment despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) on Wednesday bought an estimated $100 million on the interbank market when the zloty traded between 7.40 and 7.25 percent above the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  only cause a brief stir on the market and then, as we have seen in recent months, the zloty bounces back," said Jaroslaw Dryjski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  "Players may hold back with dollar-selling for some time, waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in, but the zloty should gain later in the day if the NBP stays away from the market," Dryjski added. \par \par \uc2  At 0805 GMT the zloty was at 7.35/7.33 percent above the parity rate against the opening's 7.38/7.24 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4080/90 to the dollar against 3.4080/110 at the start and at 1.8860/65 to the mark against 1.8850/90. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said better-than-expected inflation growth in March should further underpin the upbeat mood on Polish financial markets, stirred earlier this week by the NBP's chief comments about zloty appreciation over the longer-term. \par \par \uc2  Polish consumer prices grew 0.6 percent in March after a 1.7 percent rise in February, bringing year-on-year inflation down to 13.9 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said foreign flows into longer-term tresauries would keep the zloty poised for gains in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty still has a big potential to gain more ground," said Zbigniew Chmielewski, Treasurer at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect the market to find an equilibrium somewhere around 8.5 percent above the parity rate," Chmielewski said. \par \par \uc2  Polish short-term cash held steady around the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark drainage rate of 24 percent early on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates were at 23.85/24.10 percent against the opening's 23.80/24.00. Tomorrow/next were flat at 23.85/24.15. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4g079eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
