\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty inches higher, eyes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 14 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty strengthened slightly in early Tuesday trade and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should hold above the key seven percent level above parity after breaking resistance amid thin trade last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, that potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  might prevent players from pushing the zloty much above current levels on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty is likely to stay above 7.0 percent from parity after it smoothly broke that resistance in shallow pre-holiday trade on Friday," one foreign bank dealer in Warsaw said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) refrained from staging \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Friday's shortened session. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks the NBP bought dollars on the market when the zloty firmed to around 6.85 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP may still want to see what is going on and when the zloty rises too quickly it can again step in," a dealer in another foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the zloty was at 7.15/7.10 percent stronger than the parity rate against the opening's 7.12/6.98 percent and Friday's close 7.11/7.02 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4275/95 to the dollar against 3.4290/40 at the start and at 1.8812/22 to the mark against 1.8815/45. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Wednesday release of Polish inflation data for March was likely to set a longer-lasting trend on the local foreign exhange market after the zloty drifted mainly sideways amid often lacklustre trade for the last few weeks. \par \par \uc2  On the money market overnight rates traded at 23.85/24.00 against the opening's 23.90/24.10 percent. Tomorrow/next were at 23.85/24.05 against 23.90/24.10 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4e07hrm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
