\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty stable vs basket, market awaits flows. \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 1 (Reuters) - The zloty held steady in early trade on Wednesday but dealers said potential foreign inflows into Polish fixed rate notes at Wednesday's primary auctions would keep the local unit under upward pressure. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday may again want to buy dollars on the interbank market if the zloty firmed to resistance at around 7.0 percent stronger than parity - previously the upper end of the unit's trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty should be in a very tight range today somewhere between 6.9 and 6.6 percent from parity," said Malgorzata Sawicka, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  "Around 6.9 percent we can have a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and at 6.6 percent form parity we'll see players buying zlotys for T-bonds at today's auctions," Sawicka said. \par \par \uc2  At 0745 GMT the zloty was at 6.80/6.77 percent above the trading band centre against opening 6.83/6.72 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4485/00 to the dollar against 3.4480/20 at the start and at 1.8675/80 to the mark against 1.8665/85. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected large foreign interest at Wednesday's T-bond auctions, where the finance ministry offers a total of 1.45 billion zlotys of two-, four-and five-year fixed rate notes. The value date for the tender is April 12, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Some said, however, foreign investors may refrain from buying zlotys on Wednesday, awaiting a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which could knock the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. \par \par \uc2  "Investors may be waiting for some time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could give them good levels to enter the zloty," one Polish bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) staged no \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after buying an estimated $55 mln on the market at the previous session when the zloty was between 6.85 and 6.70 percent stronger than the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Polish short-term rates inched down early on Wednesday as the local money market remained overliquid in the first days of the new monthly reserve period, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight rates traded on Wednesday at 23.85/24.10 percent against opening 24.00/24.30 percent. Tomorrow/next were at 24.05/24.25 against 24.00/24.30 percent at the start. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4108bs2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
