\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - Central Europe stays bid. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  picked up where they left off last week, with the Czech crown pushing seven-month highs on Monday and continued demand for zlotys drawing fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Ukrainian hryvnia was little moved by early indications that Sunday's parliamentary elections showed the Communist Party was likely to win most votes. \par \par \uc2  Meantime emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed to a touch softer, with analysts expecting a period of consolidation there after recent strong gains. \par \par \uc2  "Central Europe is outperforming again and this week's EU accession talks serve as a reminder about why there's a particular edge to that story, " said a trader at a U.S. bank. "Everywhere else, there seems to be a bit of levelling-off." \par \par \uc2  Talks on European Union membership for Poland, Hungary, the Czech Republic, Slovenia, Estonia and Cyprus start on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark/Czech crown rate broke below 18.40 on Monday for the first time since last August. \par \par \uc2  The crown has been boosted in an environment of calm international markets as investors search for high yields despite underlying political uncertainty ahead of June's elections. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the next key chart support was the lows from last August about 18.26. If the mark was to breach this support, it would then return to levels not seen since just prior to last May's Czech devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occasions on Monday to sell zlotys for dollars. Regular bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to cap the zloty have failed to depress the unit. \par \par \uc2  The zloty was trading about midsession at about 6.83 percent above its parity against a basket of officially-targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , close to where it was prior to the first round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the 7.0 percent barrier looks to be a sensitive level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The only thing the NBP can realistically do here is to slow the upside," said one analyst at a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It can't really hope to depress the zloty for long because the positive fundamentals driving it higher are likely to remain in place for at least another six-to-twelve months." \par \par \uc2  Investors bid for 1.8 billion zlotys of Treasury bills at a 900 million zloty auction on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In Asia earlier, the Indonesian rupiah edged lower amid some profit-taking on its recent rally. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said sentiment toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained positive as the outcome of talks between the government and the International Monetary Fund on the country's debt restructuring are awaited. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said a deal was possible as soon as Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT \par \par \uc2     The following is a snapshot of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    ASIA\tab \par    * Indonesian rupiah\tab     8,500 per dollar bid vs 8,350 late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  in London on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Malaysian ringgit\tab     at 3.6100 per dollar from 3.56 per\par  dollar. Thai baht\tab \tab 38.00 per dollar vs 38.35. Philippine\par  peso\tab     37.20 per dollar vs 37.25.\par    * South Korean won\tab     1,382 versus 1,377.\par    * Singapore dollar\tab     1.596 per dollar versus 1.5865.\par  Taiwan dollar\tab     at 32.805 vs 32.602.\par    * Indian rupee\tab     at 39.495 per dollar vs 39.44.\par    EUROPE\tab \tab \par    * Russian rouble\tab     at 6.0885 per dollar bid vs 6.089.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's daily bid/offer rates at 6.0880/6.1240\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  versus 6.0860/6.1220.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Zloty about 6.83 percent above basket parity from 6.90/80\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  percent at the open. Mark/Czech crown\tab \tab  at 18.38 bid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  compared with 18.421.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Slovak crown 1.70 percent below basket parity versus 1.85\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  percent late Friday. Hungarian forint unchanged at 2.25 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  above its basket parity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Ukrainian hryvnia\tab     2.041 per dollar versus 2.0399.\par  Romanian leu\tab     at 8,460 per dollar versus 8,485.\par    AFRICA\tab \tab \par    * South African rand\tab     at 4.9745 per dollar vs 4.989.\par  Kenyan shilling\tab     59.85 versus 59.70.\par    LATIN AMERICA\tab \par * Mexican peso\tab   at 8.5200 per dollar vs 8.5140. Brazil's real      at 1.1360 per dollar bid vs 1.1360. ((London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110 fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3u08e73\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex