\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty touch stronger vs basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 26 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty edged up in early Thursday trade and dealers said upward pressure on the zloty should remain on Thursday despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the last two sessions. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty for the second day running on Wednesday, buying an estimated $70 million on the market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was between 6.7 and 6.4 percent from the trading band centre. \par \par \uc2  "The scenario will probably repeat itself as players will keep selling dollars and the NBP will continue to step in, but the market should be pretty calm," said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the zloty could weaken significantly as some upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains," Fiderkiewicz added. \par \par \uc2  At 0905 GMT the zloty was at 6.69/6.65 percent stronger than the parity rate against the opening's 6.66/6.56 percent. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4305/20 to the dollar against 3.4330/70 at the start and at 1.8768/74 to the mark against 1.8760/80. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty would be well supported by new capital inflows whenever it dipped out of its present range between six and seven percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect more inflows into the zloty and Polish treasuries if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened below 6.0 percent from parity," an analyst in a foreign bank in London said. \par \par \uc2  Polish short-term cash stayed below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark drainage rate at 24 percent on Thursday after the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week injected additional funds into the system. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight rates traded at 23.10/23.50 percent against the opening's 23.45/23.75. Tomorrow/next were at 23.30/23.70 against Wednesday's close of 23.50/24.10. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3q08opt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
