\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - crown rallies, zloty capped. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 915 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 25 (Reuters) - Demand for central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained robust on Wednesday, but the Czech crown and Polish zloty diverged amid conflicting signals from their central banks. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second consecutive day to sell zlotys for dollars after the zloty had quickly bounced back in the wake of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown strengthened, meantime, after vice-governor of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Jan Vit said the bank was not considering easing monetary policy any time soon as it was battling to meet its inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments caused the latest move in the crown but I'd be worried about mark/Czech about these levels," said Nick Douch, corporate risk adviser at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  "Quite apart from the disappointing inflation picture, the outcome of the June elections is looking more and more uncertain and further crown strength runs the risk of re-igniting current account problems." \par \par \uc2  Poland, on the other hand, remains attractive despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's protests, and the magnet of 20-percent-plus yields is likely to keep investors coming back, Douch said. \par \par \uc2  Despite reports of dissent within the NBP over Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at about $35 million, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold zlotys on several occasions again on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The sales started as the zloty traded near 6.75 percent above parity against an officially-targeted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the same level where it began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The zloty edged back below 6.50 percent in response to the latest wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, from 6.78/54 at the open. \par \par \uc2  "The seven percent area, which was the limit of the old band, is obviously a sensitive area for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they would want to be careful about drawing lines in the sand,' said one dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "The bulk of the foreign investment in this market is in for the interest-rate carry, not the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, and the zloty would have to be at a risk of a move back below parity before that sort of investment is deterred." \par \par \uc2  Mark/Czech, meantime, slid to test 18.50 from just above 18.60 late Tuesday as Vit's comments reinforced technical signals. Trendline resistance just above 18.64 is reinforcing the strength of the crown, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in emerging Europe, the Romanian leu firmed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars for the second time this week. \par \par \uc2  The leu had skidded to about 8,500 per dollar from 8,050 late last week as local dealers cited foreign selling of fixed income investments. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a strong grip on this market, mainly because there's very little foreign money in there," said Douch at Barclays. "But investors are fed up with the slowdown in the whole reform process and temptation is to pull out unless there is some movement." \par \par \uc2  Senior Romanian officials on Monday said the country will notify the International Monetary Fund that it accepts Article Eight of the IMF treaty relating to current account convertibility of the leu. \par \par \uc2  Turkish markets' strong performance continued on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Easing tensions between the government and the army in Turkey have boosted fixed income markets as concern about a snap election recedes and investors focus on high nominal yields and expectations of slowing inflation. \par \par \uc2  Turkish bond yields dropped 160 basis points on Wednesday, bring the fall since Friday to about 500 bp. The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold lira for dollars in two rounds on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Asia earlier, the Malaysian ringgit and the Indonesian rupiah strengthened. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was lifted as Bank Negara's latest report stressed the need to keep monetary policy tight. The rupiah was boosted amid speculation a new IMF package is imminent and amid optimism about the country's debt restructuring. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following is a snapshot of emerging markets \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. ASIA\tab \par * Indonesian rupiah\tab   8,275 per dollar bid vs 8,525 late in London on Tuesday.\par * Malaysian ringgit\tab   at 3.615 per dollar from 3.6455 per dollar on Tuesday. Thai baht\tab     38.60 per dollar vs 38.50. Philippine peso\tab   37.00 per dollar vs 36.95.\par * South Korean won\tab   1,385 versus 1,374 Tuesday.\par * Singapore dollar\tab   1.6055 per dollar versus 1.6100. Taiwan dollar\tab   at 32.60 vs 32.65.\par * Indian rupee\tab   at 39.47 per dollar vs 39.40.\par EUROPE\tab \tab \par * Russian rouble\tab   at 6.0900 per dollar bid vs 6.0835. Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's daily bid/offer rates at 6.0810/6.1200 versus 6.0780/6.1200 Tuesday.\par * Zloty about 6.49 percent above basket parity from 6.48/35 percent at the opening. Mark/Czech crown\tab      at 18.524 bid compared with 18.607 Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Slovak crown 1.97 percent below basket parity versus 2.00 percent on Tuesday. Hungarian forint at 2.23 percent above its basket parity versus 2.24 percent Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ukrainian hryvnia\tab   2.044 per dollar versus 2.0365. Romanian leu \tab  at 8,320 per dollar versus 8,475.\par AFRICA\tab \tab \par * South African rand\tab   at 4.9720 per dollar vs 4.9745. Kenyan shilling\tab   60.10 versus 59.95.\par LATIN AMERICA\tab \par * Mexican peso\tab   at 8.5300 per dollar vs 8.5300. Brazil's real    at 1.1349 per dollar bid vs 1.1345.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110 fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3p08mkm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
