\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Polish NBP walks tightrope with zloty policy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in a month to cool the zloty in what analysts said was a risky game which might lure short-term speculators. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the NBP had to slow the zloty's rise to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from climbing towards the top of its trading band - a situation which would lower the exchange rate risk and potentially spark more inflows into Poland. \par \par \uc2  "If the zloty sticks to the top of its band for long enough it starts to look like a fixed exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of high stability - like in Hungary - encouraging even more inflows," said David Mars, economist at SCB Warburg in London. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the NBP bought roughly $35 million and pushed the zloty down to 6.26/6.22 percent on the stronger side of the trading band centre from Monday's 6.76/6.70 percent close. \par \par \uc2  The zloty can trade within a 10 percent band around the parity rate. It peaked at an all-time high around 7.50 percent above parity on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Over the last month, foreign purchases of Poland's high-yielding treasuries have pushed up the zloty more than four points against its basket without sparking any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates right now are very high and pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker is going to have a potential rebound effect by bringing in more money," said Matthew Vogel, economist at Donaldson, Lufkin & Jenrette. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trigger a wave of profit-taking by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators who have opened long zloty positions over the last weeks, but analysts said that this policy might not be sustainable in the longer-term. \par \par \uc2  "They (the NBP) are trying to weaken the zloty at a small cost...but when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loses strength foreigners will again enter Polish T-bonds," said Wojciech Kowalczyk, senior dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said, however, that the Polish zloty may weaken slightly over the next several days before rebounding again amid renewed foreign interest. \par \par \uc2  "Players will probably wait two or three days to see what's going on and then we could see the zloty again close to about seven percent," said Zsolt Papp, economist at UBS in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Tuesday's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not aimed at weakening the zloty to keep the current account from deteriorating further or at setting a sure-fire resistance level for the unit. \par \par \uc2  "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have very little to do with the current account gap and targeting any nominal or real exchange rate levels and everything to do with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trying to retain its exchange rate flexibility and not being boxed into a corner," SCB Warburg's Mars added. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after it come under fire for fixing the zloty below market close on Friday and Monday - a move some market participants branded a hidden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said past fixings were weaker than market close because the Polish zloty gained mainly on speculation and not actual capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08spe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
