\par\par \b \uc2  Polish c.bank keeps interest rates, reserves flat. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 16:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 18 (Reuters) - The Monetary Policy Council decided to keep the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official interest rates, the 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate as well as the level of banks' obligatory reserves unchanged, it said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The monetary policy council at its meeting on March 18... decided that the National Bank of Poland's main interest rates will stay unchanged, the 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will also stay unchanged and so will the levels of banks' obligatory reserves," the council said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The NBP's main rates are now at 27 and 24.5 percent and the 28-day open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  minimum rate is 24 percent. \par \par \uc2  Obligatory reserves on zloty call deposits are currently at 20 percent, 11 percent on zloty term deposits and at five percent for all foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits. \par \par \uc2  The Monetary Policy Council also decided to tighten control over the way banks' calculate their obligatory reserve levels every month. \par \par \uc2  "The basis for calculating the obligatory reserve should be the arithmetical average of the funds on accounts from all working days of the previous month," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  Currently the reserves are counted on the basis of an average from only three days of the previous month - the 10th, 20th and 30th day. \par \par \uc2  "This is meant to make the obligatory reserves a more efficient instrument," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The Monetary Policy Council also decided to tighten control over the way banks' calculate their obligatory reserve levels every month. \par \par \uc2  "The basis for calculating the obligatory reserve should be the arithmetical average of the funds on accounts from all working days of the previous month," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  Currently the reserves are counted on the basis of an average from only three days of the previous month - the 10th, 20th and 30th day. \par \par \uc2  "This is meant to make the obligatory reserves a more efficient instrument," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3i096eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
