\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty -2: Some Expect Profit-Taking \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 17:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar in after-hours trading is at 3.4765 zlotys (PLN), down from Tuesday afternoon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing of PLN3.4815 and from Monday's fixing of PLN3.4895. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said foreign purchases of government bonds are helping to support the zloty. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark is at PLN1.8896, down from the afternoon fixing of PLN1.9020 and from Monday afternoon's fixing of PLN1.9095. \par \par \uc2  Ladko said the zloty's upper limit would most likely be established by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which, he said, may be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the zloty within its 20-point band around the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The zloty could eventually be weakened by a cut in key interest rates, Ladko added. But he said high demand for credit will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from cutting rates before summer. Other participants agreed. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the trading band to 20 points from 14 points two weeks ago, it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to keep the zloty from straying by much more than 2% from parity in the strong end of the band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were uncertain whether a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level would be established within the wider band. But many said it is unlikely, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to encourage greater volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Jaroslaw Krol, chief dealer at ABN Amro Bank in Warsaw, said the zloty will next attack the level of 5.5% above the midpoint and then move to 6%. 'Only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can limit the zloty,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the market will be ripe for a bout of profit-taking if the zloty gains much more. Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale, said he expects the zloty to settle in a range of between 5% and 5.2% above the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.8% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 10% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-03-98 \par \par \uc2  1607GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3a023xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
