\par\par \b \uc2  Foreign-charged zloty seen setting new highs. \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 10 (Reuters) - The zloty set a new all-time high on Tuesday and dealers said continuing foreign interest in Polish longer-term fixed income instruments would keep the unit on a steady rise in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign demand for Polish debt instruments has slowed to a certain extent, but strong interest in longer-term bonds is still there, so I see no reason why the zloty should weaken," said Ryszard Bublik, dealer at Nomura International in London. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended on Tuesday at 5.17/5.11 percent from the parity rate against Monday's close of 4.84/4.79 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.4800/25 to the dollar against 3.4900/20 on Monday and at 1.9020/30 to the mark against 1.9086/94. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the zloty to drift slowly towards 5.5 percent from parity in the next few days after breaking the strong psychological resistance of five percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Upbeat mood will keep the zloty strong and any weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a good buying oportunity," said Robert Hryciuk, dealer at Bank of America Polska SA. "I think now the market sees new levels for the zloty at around 5.5 percent." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) might still refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the zloty's ongoing appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stay quiet for a while to see how far the market want to push the zloty," Nomura's Bublik said. \par \par \uc2  "Rates are high and they are going to be attractive for some time so I don't think people are too worried about whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not. There is the natural pull for the zloty to go strong," he added. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day deposits stayed above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's drainage rates of 24 percent and overnight ratwes closed the day at 24.25/24.70 against the opening's 24.50/24.70 percent. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow/next ended the session at 24.65/24.75 percent against 24.40/24.65 percent at the start. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du3a00cfi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
