\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty hits new highs on band widening expectations. \b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The zloty jumped against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in early Wednesday trade on market expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy council may widen the daily trading band and allow the unit to rise. \par \par \uc2  "What is happening now is a result of pure speculation as the market tries to guess what decisions the Monetary Policy Council could announce today," said Malgorzata Sawicka, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (RPP), setting monetary and exchange rate policies, may want to widen the zloty's trading band to plus/minus 15 percent from the current plus/minus seven percent. \par \par \uc2  "Although they could decide to extend the zloty's band, it remains to be seen whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would then let the zloty rise towards, say, four percent (from parity)," Handlowy's Sawicka said. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the makret to cap the zloty's rise at around 2.2 percent firmer than the parity rate -- set daily against the basket of five western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a devaluation factor. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT the zloty hit a 10-month high at 2.94/2.91 percent firmer than the parity rate against the opening's 2.62/2.49 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.5220/30 to the dollar against 3.5290/40 at the start and at 1.9544/50 to the mark against 1.9640/65. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said potential profit-taking later in the day could limit the speculative zloty rise on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty has a chance to test even three percent from parity today if the morning madness continues, but as there were some signs of profit-taking already yesterday, the market may find its equilibrium somewhere between 2.5 and three percent," one foreign bank dealer in Warsaw said. \par \par \uc2  On the money market early one-day deposits inched down on Wednesday due to large cash surpluses on the market in the last days of the February reserve period. \par \par \uc2  "(Short-term) rates will probably continue a downward slide until the end of this reserve period as banks have plenty of cash," said Aleksandra Watroba, money market dealer at Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight rates traded at 22.30/22.45 percent against the opening's 22.35/22.65 and tomorrow/next were at 22.20/22.50 against 22.35/22.65. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2p0143o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
