\par\par \b \uc2  EARLY ZLOTY STABLE, EYES HIGHER GROUND. \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The zloty held relatively steady in early Monday trade, but dealers said potential foreign flows into Polish Treasury-bills at Monday's primary tender may keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under upward pressure later in the day. \par \par \uc2  "The trend for a stronger zloty remains and nothing, for now, seems to be able to undermine it. We can expect foreign capital to flow into the market," said Witold Wozniak, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Deutsche Bank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected average T-bill yields to fall to around secondary market levels at today's one billion zloty auction, with the benchmark 52-week bill seen sliding to around 21.8 percent against an average of 22.61 at the previous tender. \par \par \uc2  "T-bill yields will probably have to fall further, perhaps to around 20 percent, if capital flows and upward pressure on the zloty were to weaken," Deutsche's Wozniak said. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT the zloty was at 2.24/2.21 percent from the trading band centre against the opening's 2.28/2.20 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.5655/65 to the dollar against 3.5641/71 at the start and at 1.9555/65 to the mark against 1.9549/64. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so as to prevent a rise in the foreign-charged zloty in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at nearly every trading session for the last two weeks. \par \par \uc2  "With a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high interest rates it's hard to stop the foreign capital influx, but the NBP may still step in (with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) until longer-term steps are taken," said Jacek Wasilewski, chief dealer at Vereinsbank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expected the NBP's Monetary Policy Council (RPP), which started work last week, to discuss issues of exchange rate policy at its next meeting, scheduled for Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the money market early one-day deposits held stable on Monday and overnight rates traded at 22.90/23.00 against the opening's 22.70/23.20. \par \par \uc2  Early tomorrow/next were at 22.80/23.20 against Friday's close 21.00/22.40. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2n00lhz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
