\par\par \b \uc2  POLISH ZLOTY WEAKENS VS BASKET, BUT MOOD UNCHANGED. \b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The zloty weakened on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated 30 million German marks on the market but dealers said continued foreign interest in Polish treasuries would support the unit in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "It will probably be a very similar day tomorrow. When the zloty firms to about 2.2 percent from parity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will again step in and will try to stop its rise," said Jacek Wasilewski, chief dealer at Vereinsbank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) twice \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy marks on Thursday when the zloty firmed above 2.15 from its basket parity rate. \par \par \uc2  "Generally, trade here has been dull for the last few days because when banks want to make a major deal they either wait for the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  later at the fixing," Wasilewski said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended at 2.20/2.16 percent from the trading band centre against Wednesday's close of 2.25/2.21 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.5585/95 to the dollar against 3.5630/40 on Wednesday and at 1.9560/70 to the mark against 1.9505/14. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said foreign capital would continue to seep into Polish T-bills and T-bonds, although some yields had already fallen by more than two percentage points since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 52-week T-bill traded at around 21.80 percent in Thursday secondary trade against an average of 24.16 percent at the first primary auction this year on January 5. \par \par \uc2  "T-bill yields would have to fall by another two percent to make the papers unattractive," said Andrew Kenningham, analyst at Merrill Lynch in London. "When they are around 20 or 20.5 percent people may start to find them less interesting." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors had also entered Polish two- and five-year fixed rate notes, which traded on Thursday around 21.40/21.10 percent and 19.80/19.30 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  "So long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains the ceiling (on the zloty) at between 2.0 and 2.5 percent above the parity rate foreign capital will continue to flow in," Merrill Lynch's Kenningham said. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day depos closed at relatively low levels on Thursday even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 2.5 billion zlotys worth of its NBP-bills. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates ended the session at 22.00/22.25 against the opening's 21.90/22.40. Tomorrow/next closed at 22.00/22.70 against 21.95/22.40 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2j00keo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
