\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY INCHES UP AS C.BANK REFRAINS FROM DLR-BUYING. \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty gained some ground in lacklustre trade on Monday but dealers expected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to liven up on Tuesday if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again refrained from staging dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) staged no \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it bought a total of $600 million over the course of six consecutive trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  "Trade may be more interesting tomorrow if banks decide to start selling dollars directly on the market and not wait for the NBP to step in agian," said Malgorzata Sawicka, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended on Monday at 2.18/2.17 percent above the parity rate against Friday's close of 2.13/2.08 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.5535/40 to the dollar against 3.5590/10 on Friday and at 1.9528/32 to the mark against 1.9490/00. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the zloty to continue its upward climb against its basket parity as foreigners paid for some of the T-bills bought at Monday's one billion zloty primary auction. \par \par \uc2  "The market may want to test higher \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels as demand for the zloty remains, even though it's not so strong as it was recently," said Pawel Gajewski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Westdeutsche Landesbank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  According to local dealers' estimates foreign bids amounted to $350-400 million (1.2-1.4 billion zlotys) against total investor demand of 3.98 billion zlotys at Monday's tender. \par \par \uc2  The average yield of the benchmark 52-week T-bill, mostly sought by foreign investors, fell to 22.61 percent from 23.20 percent at the previous tender last Monday. \par \par \uc2  Polish one-day cash remained below \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage rates on Monday as last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumped large amounts of zlotys into the system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed at 21.00/22.00 percent against the opening's 22.00/22.45 percent. Tomorrow/next ended the day at 22.60/23.05 percent against 22.10/22.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2g00jmj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
