\par\par \b \uc2  NEW POLISH  \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK \highlight\uc2  COUNCIL FACES HARD CHOICES. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Pawel Kozlowski \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Poland's new Monetary Policy Council will face tough decisions when it meets for the first time this week amid a flood of foreign capital which sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Political squabbles delayed establishment of the 10-member council responsible for monetary and exchange rate policies. This has the potential to limit the scope of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responses to market trends as from the start of this year. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks foreign capital has poured into Poland's markets and put strong upward pressure on the zloty, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) bought some $600 million on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last six working days alone. But its actions did little to reverse zloty gains and drew criticism from some economists. \par \par \uc2  "If the NBP continues with its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market will remain unbalanced, money supply and inflation will grow but the zloty will strengthen anyhow," said Krzysztof Rybinski, chief analyst at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said fast growing domestic demand and a large current account gap would probably keep the Monetary Policy Council (RPP) from cutting high official interest rates until at least the middle of the year. \par \par \uc2  "The rate of credit growth has decelerated but is still pretty high so the answer is to be conservative on rate cuts and it is not clear the economy has slowed down sufficiently yet," said Arnab Das, analyst at JP Morgan in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the RPP was more likely to modify the exchange rate regime to make zloty investments more risky. \par \par \uc2  "The RPP may change its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy either by widening the trading band or changing day-to-day management of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," JP Morgan's Das said. \par \par \uc2  Currently the zloty is allowed to trade within a 14 percent daily band centred on the parity rate. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it may expand the corridor to plus/minus 15 percent around the parity early in 1998. \par \par \uc2  This move may not be effective as it is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  which limit the actual trading band and not the outer limits of the band itself. \par \par \uc2  "In practice, the widening of the band will only have a psychological effect, if any. It is clear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want the zloty to strengthen too much and will limit gains," ING's Rybinski said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also stop announcing the daily central parity rate -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band mid-point -- which would make \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels less predictable for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. \par \par \uc2  They said the RPP would probably also have to slow the zloty's crawling devaluation rate of one percent per month against a basket of Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second quarter of 1998, so as to limit its inflationary effects. \par \par \uc2  The 1998 budget envisages a 10 percent zloty devaluation during the course of this year, which would translate into about 0.8 percent per month. But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said that the budget figure was only indicative. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a slowdown of the crawling devaluation would attract even more foreign capital to various Polish securities, which were backed by a generally healthy economy. \par \par \uc2  "The strength of the zloty comes from the country's sound fundamentals," said Krzysztof Bledowski, chief analyst at WoodCommerz in Warsaw. "It is a mix of soaring stock prices, high-yielding treasuries and flows from privatisation." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the first RPP meeting was scheduled for February 17, the same day that Poland's president was due to appoint the final three members of the Council and his candidate for the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The term of the current president Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz expires on March 4 and a new chief has to be proposed by the president and then accepted by parliament. \par \par \uc2  The ruling right-wing coalition's politicians have said Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz had a very high chance of staying for a second six-year term. REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2g00jil\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
