\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Dealer -2: DEM10 Mln Bought \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1998\par 14:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, buying Deutsche Marks for zlotys at the level of 1.9505 zlotys (PLN), a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought DEM10 million. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer at a major Western bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought dollars for zlotys at the level of PLN3.5540. The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $10 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought marks and dollars when the zloty reached about 2.2% above the midpoint of the trading band. After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the zloty was trading at around 2.15% above the midpoint of the band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At around 1316 GMT, the dollar was quoted at PLN3.5590, up from PLN3.5485 at the opening and from Thursday's fixing of 3.5470. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9505, down from PLN1.9540 at the opening\par and from Thursday's fixing of 1.9560.\par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; +48 22 622 2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1331GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2d019pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
