\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Up In Early Trade,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1998\par 10:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was higher against the dollar in early trading Thursday as dealers braced themselves for another round of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was trading at around 2.05% above the midpoint of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  Wojciech Trzepizur, dealer at Bank Rozwoju Eksportu, said the zloty was not yet strong enough to 'provoke' another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But he said if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthens, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the zloty's rise by buying dollars for the last four trading sessions in a row. \par \par \uc2  Around 0915 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5530 zlotys (PLN), down from Wednesday's fixing of PLN3.5585. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9560, up from Wednesday's fixing of PLN1.9535. \par \par \uc2  Malgorzata Sawicka, dealer at Bank Handlowy, said the market was fairly stable in early trade but said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still possible. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6290 and for the mark at PLN1.9963. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 2.1% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.20% and\par 23.20%.\par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0940GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2c016oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
