\par\par \b \uc2  EARLY ZLOTY TOUCH FIRMER, WAITS FOR INFLOWS. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The zloty inched up in early Thursday trade and dealers said more foreign-inflows could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  later today. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign players keep selling dollars and enter Polish securities and we expect more foreign flows today and thus more clashes with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) bought an estimated $60 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, the fourth consecutive day the bank staged a dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT the zloty was at 2.12/2.08 percent above the trading band centre against the opening's 2.10/2.04 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.5510/30 to the dollar against 3.5525/45 at the start and at 1.9547/53 to the mark against 1.9547/57. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the zloty's gains could be limited on Thursday as players rebuild dollar-positions shortened for the long weekend holiday in the United States. \par \par \uc2  Polish one-day depos have kept below \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage rates since the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Banks have large fund surpluses at the moment after the NBP pumped so much cash into the market recently," one money market dealer in a Polish bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term rates may stay low for the next few days if dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight rates traded at 22.65/22.95 against the opening's 22.60/22.90 and tomorrow/next were quoted flat at 22.70/23.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2c00i71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
