\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty firms vs basket, seen steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The zloty firmed against the basket in Thursday quiet trade and dealers expected the local unit to stay relatively stable on Friday, with foreign players staying on the sidelines after strong entry early in the week. \par \par \uc2  "There was almost no trading today and the market was very calm. We will probably have to wait for next primary auctions, which could give a boost to the zloty," said Bogdan Stepkowski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) continued with its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and bought an estimated $10 million just before the close of the session. \par \par \uc2  "On the one side there are foreign investors and on the other there is the NBP and so the zloty remains flat," ING's Stepkowski said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed on Thursday at 2.18/2.14 percent from the trading band centre against Wednesday's 2.10/2.04 percent. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 3.5460/80 to the dollar against 3.5570/90 on Wednesday and at 1.9554/59 to the mark against 1.9524/34. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said foreign capital influx into Poland would increase in the next few days, propelling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fresh clashes with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is the result of interest rates being still quite high, which makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  very attractive and also the result of market expectations that the rate of the crawling peg would be reduced," said Miranda Xafa, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Salomon Smith Barney in London. \par \par \uc2  The zloty is currently devalued against a basket of five foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by one percent a month. \par \par \uc2  Polish one-day cash remained below \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage rates on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected large amounts of zlotys through its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed at 22.70/23.30 against the opening's 22.60/22.90. Tomorrow/next ended the day at 22.70/23.30 percent 22.70/23.00. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2c05cdv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
