\par\par \b \uc2  EARLY ZLOTY STABLE VS BASKET, MAY INCH UP. \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty held steady in early Wednesday trade but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again step in with market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so as to stop the unit's potential rise if more foreign capital entered Poland. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) staged the third consecutive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the zloty just above two percent from the trading band centre. \par \par \uc2  "We can expect another battle with the NBP today, even though foreign flows are not as big as they were last week," said Mateusz Bieniek, dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "As long as some demand for the zloty holds the NBP will step in to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak," Bieniek added. \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT the zloty was at 2.16/2.14 percent above the trading band centre against the opening's 2.18/2.12 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.5460/70 to the dollar against 3.5420/50 at the start and at 1.9572/77 to the mark against 1.9590/00. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said foreign investors might refrain from larger zloty-purchases in the next few days after their strong entry last Friday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $400 million to cap the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreaciation. \par \par \uc2  "Foreigners have recently bought larger amounts of zlotys and they may want to take a breath, but probably not for long," said Jacek Wasilewski, chief dealer at Vereinsbank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  One-day deposits held below \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage rates in early trade on Wednesday but dealers expected rates to inch up on the back of anticipated large-scale open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight and tomorrow/next rates traded at 22.90/23.10 percent against the opening's 22.65/23.15 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2b00i72\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
