\par\par \b \uc2  FOREIGN-CHARGED ZLOTY SHADE WEAKER, EYES C.BANK. \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The zloty weakened against its basket parity on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again bought dollars on the market and dealers said foreign inflows into treasuries would provoke more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "Right now, the zloty seems to be everybody's bet and I don't know of anybody who is not long on the zloty. I wouldn't be surprised if you see more flows coming," said Zsolt Papp, emerging markets economist at UBS in London. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) staged an estimated $60-million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth consecutive day to kept the zloty just above two percent firmer than parity. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps on buying dollars at around two percent (from parity), basically for sure, it is almost a safe bet (to enter the zloty)," Papp added. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.10/2.04 percent from the parity rate against Tuesday's 2.15/2.12 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.5570/90 to the dollar against 3.5426/40 on Tuesday and at 1.9524/34 to the mark against 1.9561/67. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said foreign investor sentiment towards Poland was strengthened further after deputy finance minister Jaroslaw Bauc said the ministry wanted the country's budget balanced around the year 2001. \par \par \uc2  "Our absolutely top goal, above all others, is to balance the budget...our ambitious plans are to do it in three years so that in the year 2001 we have no deficit," Bauc told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day deposits stayed below \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage rates due to large cash surpluses on the back of recent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed on Wednesday at 22.70/23.05 against the opening's 22.65/23.15 and tomorrow/next ended at 22.75/23.15 against 22.65/23.35. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 680 million zlotys of its seven-day NBP-bills, whose average yield was 23.49 percent, up from 23.44 percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2b00hjb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
