\par\par \b \uc2  Poland  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Trader Seens A 'Warning Signal' \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1998\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars for zlotys at late morning at the level of 3.5435 zlotys (PLN), a dealer at a major Western bank said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $10 million. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at PLN3.5435, down from PLN3.5473 at the opening and from Monday's fixing of PLN3.5445. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was quoted at PLN1.9580, up from PLN1.9530 at the opening and from Monday's fixing of PLN1.9545. \par \par \uc2  Dealers at several other banks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been calling them to check their bids on the dollar, but hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at those banks. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sending a warning signal,' that it wouldn't allow the zloty to rise to more than 2% above the mid-point of the trading band, said a dealer at a Polish bank. \par \par \uc2  The dealer noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time when the dollar was falling against the mark, thus reinforcing a market trend rather than fighting it. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par is devalued at a rate of 1.0% per month. It is theoretically allowed to\par fluctuate within plus or minus 7.0% of the central parity rate, but in\par practice the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  enforces a much tighter band.\par -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1031GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2a013t5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
