\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY GAINS, SET TO BATTLE C.BANK  \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 10 (Reuters) - The zloty gained some ground on Tuesday and dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would continue its struggle with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as foreign capital seeped into \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's high-yielding treasuries. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign flows are not as large as they were last Friday but foreigners keep entering the zloty," said Pawel Gajewski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at West LB Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  According to market estimates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $60 million zlotys through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and $520 million since last Friday in order to keep the zloty weak. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can push the unit below two percent from parity, but only for a brief moment as a strong pro-zloty sentiment remains," Gajewski added. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended on Tuesday at 2.15/2.12 percent from the parity rate against Monday's close of 2.07/2.02 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.5426/40 to the dollar against 3.5440/60 on Monday and at 1.9561/67 to the mark against 1.9540/50. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the zloty traded roughly around 2.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar-selling sentiment intensifies (because foreigners can enter the zloty at more attractive levels)," said Leszek Szafranek, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  "This trend may continue for quite a long time as Poland's fundamentals are fine and this attracts investors," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said large-scale foreign buying, estimated at between $300 and $400 million so far this week, knocked down yields of Polish longer-term treasuries in secondary trade. \par \par \uc2  "Foreigners buy up all the longer-term papers they can get grab on the market and yields keep falling down," one Polish bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 52-week T-bill yield fell to 22.90/22.80 percent on Tuesday from a 23.20 average at Monday's tender. \par \par \uc2  Five-year fixed rate bonds traded at 20.90/20.50 percent and two-year papers at 23.10/22.90 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign flows into Poland may actually increase soon," said Vlad Sobell, senior economist at Daiwa in London, "As Poland is a success story in Central Europe at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Polish one-day deposits remained below the 23.55 percent drainage rates as Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  NBP-bill sales were not able to soak up all of the market's overliquidity caused by the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  marekt \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed at 22.40/23.00 against the opening's 21.80/22.50 and tomorrow/next ended at 22.60/23.00 against 21.80/22.50 at the start. \par \par \uc2  The NBP sold 2.75 billion zlotys worth of bills, with the 7-day bill yielding 23.44 percent and the 182-day 23.50. \par \par \uc2  ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2a00hoz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
