\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Lower Vs Basket Following  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1998\par 11:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was lower against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Monday following renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0957 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5425 zlotys (PLN), up from PLN3.5395 at the opening and from Friday's fixing of PLN3.5260. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9588, up from PLN1.9535 at the opening but down from Friday's fixing of PLN1.9655. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to buy dollars for zlotys when the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to move higher than 2.2% above the mid point of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $25 million from one Polish bank at the level of PLN3.5350, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought dollars for zlotys at another major Western bank at the level of PLN3.5450, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said upward pressure on the zloty continues despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to keep the zloty to about 2% above the mid-point of the band. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6154 and for the mark at PLN1.9980. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 2.02% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 1.96% above/below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 23.00% and 23.50%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1019GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du29013rg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
