\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY HEADS FOR WAR WITH POLISH C.BANK -ANALYSTS. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 6 (Reuters) - Recently timid foreign investors threw caution to the wind on Friday, flooding Poland's markets with capital and putting the zloty on a collision course with a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  determined to halt its rise, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP), which bought an estimated $400 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, would be tested again over the next days as foreigners continue to flock into Poland's attractive securites. \par \par \uc2  "Until interest rates come down, and if the NBP continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent (the zloty reaching) equilibrium levels, there is no reason why this trend cannot be sustained," said Robert Beange, economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  "This is always the case with inflows, that when you try to prevent what is going on then you ultimately prolong the experience," Beange added. \par \par \uc2  Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of its biggest ever, forced down the foreign-charged zloty nearly half a point against the parity rate -- the mid-point of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.07/2.01 percent on the stronger side of parity, against Thursday's close 2.50/2.46 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said signs of recovery in Asian and other emerging markets fuelled foreign investor appetite for Poland, whose sound economic fundamentals and high rates made it one of the best investments in its risk class. \par \par \uc2  "Two percent is definitely a good support level for the zloty...and the recovery in Asia is continuing and that helps the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making it a great buy," Jesper Dannesboe, emerging market economist at ABN-Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty in a bid to secure exports growth and keep favourable trade balance trends intact. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been consistent and today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate given that \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not completely out of the woods in the balance of payments," said Ehsun Khan, analyst at Morgan Stanley in London. \par \par \uc2  Poland's current account deficit amounted to less than 3.5 percent of gross domestic product in 1997 as positive export figures late last year lowered the gap below expectations. \par \par \uc2  The current account gap is expected to widen to some 4.5 to 5.5 percent of GDP in 1998, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that even though Poland's Monetary Policy Council, which was supposed take control the country's monetary policy from the start of 1998, has not yet been formed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to take necessary measures if needed. \par \par \uc2  "So far five of the council's 10 members have been appointed, so together with the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the council can make decisions if necessary," said one senior analyst at a Polish bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials did not want to comment on the issue but the press office said that it expected the first council meeting to take place around February 17. \par \par \uc2  The creation of the council, which will comprise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president and three members each picked by parliament's lower house, Senate and the president, has been stalled by disagreement over candidates within Poland's ruling right-centre coalition. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2600uez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
