\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Higher; Fears Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Grow \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1998\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty is higher against the dollar on Thursday in quiet trading as dealers predicted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be likely. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zlotys was trading at around 2.45% above the midpoint of the trading bank, a rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5138 zlotys (PLN), down from Wednesday's fixing of PLN3.5240. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9500, down from Wednesday's fixing of PLN1.9435. \par \par \uc2  'There's little activity on the market,' said Andrzej Fiderkieiwicz, dealer at Societe Generale. He said investors were waiting and watching the market closely in case the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Marek Cherubin, dealer at Creditanstalt, said it was difficult to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of its unpredictability. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6017 and for the mark at PLN1.9994. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 2.4% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.5% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 24.00% and\par 24.50%.\par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0936GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du25010bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
