\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY SEEN IGNORING  \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK \highlight\uc2 , TO TEST UPSIDE. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Pawel Kozlowski \par \uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty lost nearly half a percentage point on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged its largest dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in months, but analysts said foreign capital flows would soon fuel another zloty rise. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) bought more than $100 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to market estimates, and knocked the zloty down from an eight-month high around 2.55 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "Give me one single reason for the zloty to be weak if the fundamentals are strong and foreign investors keep buying Poland's high-yielding treasuries," said Zbigniew Chmielewski, Treasurer at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Poland's solid economic growth, a smaller than expected current account deficit in 1997 and high interest rates made the country a prime destination for capital inflows in 1998 once the storm over many emerging markets calmed. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty will keep getting stronger and stronger and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only slow this rise. The next \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come around three percent (from parity)," he said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.17/2.09 percent on the stronger side of the parity rate on Monday against Friday's 2.09/2.00. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.5495/25 to the dollar against 3.5410/30 on Friday and at 1.9375/90 to the mark against 1.9435/60. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would probably refrain from testing today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels over the next few days as players were more cautious about pushing the zloty higher in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  "A short-term resistance level was formed (around 2.5 percent) and it will take some time for the zloty to break it, but upward pressure continues," said Jan Mieczkowski, Treasurer at Deutsche Bank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  "It remains to be seen where the zloty's longer-term ceiling forms, but without doubt, it is not where the zloty was trading on Monday," he added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that continuing foreign demand for Polish longer-term treasuries would keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the steady rise in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty can strengthen back to 2.5 or even 3.0 percent as you have a bond auction coming up this week and I would expect to see increased foreign demand again," said Ryszard Bublik, fixed income dealer at Nomura International in London. \par \par \uc2  Last week foreign investors bought more than 400 million zlotys of Polish 12-percent fixed rate notes, due February 12, 2002, at a 600 million zloty primary auction. \par \par \uc2  "Poland is now the leading country in the region and people are more optimistic about Poland than they had ever been," Bublik added. \par \par \uc2  This Wednesday the finance ministry will offer 1.2 billion zlotys of its two- and five-year fixed rate notes. \par \par \uc2  ((Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du2200t7w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
