\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Gains Vs Basket;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen Likely \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1998\par 11:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty continued to strengthen on Wednesday, moving up to nearly 2.2% above the midpoint of the trading band, or the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'It's a level at which the (National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Marek Lusztyn, a dealer at Bank Handlowy. 'Everybody is sitting and waiting for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Jan. 20, selling zlotys for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Wednesday that they didn't expect the zloty to gain much more. 'I don't expect foreign investors to enter the market right now with the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hanging in the air,' said Konrad Zarebski, a dealer at Powszechny Bank Kredytowy. \par \par \uc2  Around 0937 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5145 zlotys (PLN), down from PLN3.5205 at the opening but up from Tuesday's fixing of PLN3.5015. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9540, up from PLN1.9505 at the opening but down from Tuesday's fixing of PLN1.9600. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.5966 and for the mark at PLN1.9959. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 2.28% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.1% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 25.20% and 25.60%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1007GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1s00pck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
