\par\par \b \uc2  POLISH  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  LIBERALISATION IN H2 1998-FINMIN. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 28 (Reuters) - Poland's new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  law liberalising zloty trade should take effect in the second half of this year, Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "I think in the first half of this year the law will be adopted in parliament and in the second half there will be the major liberalisation," Balcerowicz told Reuters Financial Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  The zloty is now fully convertible only domestically and cannot be used as an invoice \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign trade of goods or services. \par \par \uc2  The bill would allow for zloty payments for goods and services purchased abroad but would keep many restrictions on capital flows and give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  large powers of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  law might make the zloty more vulnerable to a speculative attack, Balcerowicz said there were various theories. \par \par \uc2  "But it is beyond doubt that we have to liberalise according to our agreements with the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development and the European Union." \par \par \uc2  "The best response to would-be dangers is a prudent macro-economic policy and accelerated structural reforms," he added. \par \par \uc2  Balcerowicz, now steering a tight 1998 budget through parliament with a projected budget deficit of 1.5 percent of gross domestic product, said he hoped this would curb the flow of hot money. \par \par \uc2  "We are reducing the budget deficit so there is hope that the inflow of speculative capital will be less," Balcerowicz said. \par \par \uc2  The new centre-right government is placing priority on stabilisation of the economy after four-years of rule by the previous coalition led by ex-communists, and on pressing ahead with major privatisations and structural reforms including an overhaul of the pensions system. \par \par \uc2  Balcerowicz said he hoped for an inflow of foreign direct investment to Poland next year and did not think investors would be discouraged by troubles in other emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  "I am sure that serious investors can distinguish healthy tigers from sick tigers and I would include Poland's economy among the healthy tigers," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Anthony Barker, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130du1s00rwl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
