\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Up In Nervous Trading After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1998\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty (PLN) was slightly higher against the dollar in nervous trading Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was trading at around 1.95% above the midpoint of its trading band, down from around 2.15% during morning trade Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'Foreign investors are not opening short positions because they're afraid that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again,' said Mateusz Bieniek, dealer at Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  Around 0927 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5480 zlotys, up from PLN3.5450 in early trading but down from Tuesday's fixing of PLN3.5500. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at PLN1.9375, up from early trading of PLN1.9340 and Tuesday's fixing of 1.9300. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  'was a signal for the market that a trading level of above 2% is not acceptable for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Tomasz Wlad. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty stayed below the 2% level but added that trading would probably remain nervous through the day. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLN3.6174 and for the mark at PLN1.9726. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 1.9% below its parity rate, and the mark 1.8% below. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate 7% either side of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 25.00% and 25.50%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0952GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1l00k03\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
