\par\par \b \uc2  REPEAT: Poland's Zloty Lower, Seen Rising On Dollar Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 1998\par 18:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was slightly lower against the dollar Monday but dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise on dollar selling by domestic and foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the zloty was trading around 2% above the midpoint of the trading band, up from around 1.8% during Friday's trading. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, the dollar was at 3.5450 zlotys, down from Friday's fixing of 3.5500 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9200 zlotys, down from Friday's fixing of 1.9400 zlotys. Dealers said the mark's drop was caused by the dollar's rise against the mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was nervous because of the high fixing of the zloty against the dollar by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is asking questions about the rates,' said Tomasz Wlad, dealer at AmerBank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently being fixing the zloty at a high rate against the dollar to prevent banks from selling zlotys at a profit to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the fixing after pushing the zloty up during the trading session. \par \par \uc2  Marek Cherubin, dealer at Creditanstalt, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again Monday at the fixing. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.6136 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9708 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 1.9% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.6% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 26.00% and 26.50%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1727GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1j00i8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
