\par\par \b \uc2  POLISH NEW  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  LAW IN NEXT FEW MONTHS -FINMIN. \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Poland's new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  law further liberalising zloty trade should be in place in the next few months, Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz said. \par \par \uc2  "The outline of the law is ready and it is ( the implementation) is a question of the next few months," Balcerowicz told Reuters in a Monday interview. \par \par \uc2  The zloty is now fully convertible only domestically and cannot be used as an invoice \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign trade of goods or services. \par \par \uc2  The new bill would allow for zloty payments for goods and services purchased abroad but would keep many restrictions on capital flows and give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  large powers of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the liberalisation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  law would not make the zloty more vulnerable to a speculative attack, Balcerowicz said: \par \par \uc2  "Not if we retain control over the liberalisation. What's more, the liberalisation is another reason why we should conduct stable macroeconomic policies." \par \par \uc2  Balcerowicz's cabinet has set the stabilisation of the economy after a four-year rule of the previous ex-communist and peasant coalition as its main task for next year. It has said that the previous government did not take advantage of the fast growth to complete market reforms and encouraged living beyond one's means. \par \par \uc2  Balcerowicz said he expected a large inflow of foreign direct investment to Poland next year as Western enterpreneurs appreciate the country's sound economic fundamentals against less impressive performance of other emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  ((Jan Strupczewski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtcf013b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
