\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Mkts  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down But Steadier; Zloty Hit Hard \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 15:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (Dow Jones)--Emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe, the Middle East and Africa were lower Tuesday, reflecting the turmoil in international financial markets that followed the record 554-point decline in the Dow Jones Industrial Average Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, the speed of the decline appeared to be easing by midday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty experienced the sharpest fall, declining 2.5% against the dollar. But an official of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'We don't see any reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being,' said Krzysztof Majczuk, director of the Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Department. 'Of course, we are watching the market closely.' \par \par \uc2  The zloty fell as foreign investors withdrew from zloty-denominated Treasury bills, bonds and other assets. \par \par \uc2  Around 1312 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 3.5560 zlotys, up from Monday's fixing of 3.4680 zlotys. The zloty dropped to about 3.7% below the midpoint of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, compared with about 0.14% below the mid-point late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Some market observers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the zloty within its trading band of plus or minus 7% around the central parity rate, which is pegged to a basket of Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'At some point we could see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  come in and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the zloty,' said David Simmonds, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Citibank in London. But he said it was unlikely the zloty would be devalued. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  10-28-97 \par \par \uc2  09:02 AM \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020011009dtas00mgc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
