\par\par \b \uc2  Poland Zloty Gains Vs Basket After New Premier's Designation \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty continued to gain ground against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on news of progress on forming a coalition government and the designation of a new prime minister. \par \par \uc2  The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  approached the level of 1.5% above the midpoint of its trading band - a level at which dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0942 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4078 zlotys, down from 3.4130 zlotys at the opening but up from Friday's fixing of 3.4020 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9225 zlotys, up from 1.9228 zlotys at the opening and from Friday's fixing of 1.9310 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Pawel Gajewski, assistant treasury manager at Creditanstalt, said foreign investors, heartened by the smooth transition of power to a new government in Poland, continued to buy government securities. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, President Aleksander Kwasniewski designated Jerzy Buzek, the candidate of Solidarity Electoral Action, to be Poland's next prime minister. \par \par \uc2  Also on Friday, Solidarity Electoral Action and the centrist Freedom Union party said they had reached an agreement in principle on forming a coalition government and on the division of ministerial and other key administrative and legislative posts. \par \par \uc2  'It looks like the pressure to sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fairly strong,' Gajewski said. \par \par \uc2  He predicted the zloty would continue to gain ground and reach the level of 1.5% above parity, possibly triggering \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.4618 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9511 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 1.56% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 1.47% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 23.80% and 24.15%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz; 48-22 622-2766; cwellisz@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-10-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1005GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtak07wc4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
