\par\par \b \uc2  EARLY ZLOTY INCHES UP VS BASKET, SEEN STABLE. \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The zloty inched up in early trade on Friday and dealers expected the local unit to stay stable within its trading range of 1.3-1.4 percent from parity for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty eyes trading in between 1.3 and 1.4 percent above parity as on the one hand there are constant inflows from privatisation deals and on the other some foreigners have started taking profits," said Mateusz Bieniek, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the zloty was at 1.44/1.41 percent form parity against the opening's 1.42/1.34 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.4000/10 to the dollar against the opening's 3.4000/30 and at 1.9337/42 to the mark against 1.9345/60. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a decisive National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could knock the zloty's down, but most did not expect any NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers saw Poland's current political situation having little imidiate impact on the zloty as the market had already discounted the large role of pro-market Freedom Union in Poland's next cabinet with the election winning Solidarity. \par \par \uc2  On Friday little-known academic Jerzy Buzek is widely expected to get designated as Poland's next prime minister. \par \par \uc2  "Many positive things have already happened and some foreign capital has flowed into the market. The market seems willing to give the new government a chance," said one dealer from a foreign bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  On the money-market one-day deposits eased slightly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from staging any open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, but remained high as banks wanted to place cash for the week-end to increase average reserve levels. \par \par \uc2  Early overnight depos were at 23.40/24.00 percent against the opening's 23.60/24.00. Tomorrow/next rates were at 23.60/24.30 percent against 23.60/23.90. \par \par \uc2  -- Pawel Kozlowski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtah00mw4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
