\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY STEADILY INCHES UP, C.BANK SILENT. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Oct 14 (Reuters) - Foreign inflows into Polish securities and payments for privatisation deals have kept the zloty bullish on Tuesday though the possibility of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowed down the unit's gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Strong interest in the Polish market remains and foreign players need the zloty to pay for securities and stakes of privatised firms," said Mariusz Wituszynski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Kredyt Bank SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 1.37/1.33 percent from the trading band centre on Tuesday against Monday's 1.26/1.23 percent as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it despite expectations. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.3935/45 to the dollar, against 3.3950/65 on Monday and at 1.9350/65 to the mark, against 1.9360/65. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said demand for the zloty was strong enough to push the zloty yet higher but uncertainty over the potential National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the market cautious. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are now waiting for the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  happens they sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the post-trade fixing," said Piotr Czyzewski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  The NBP was idle on Tuesday for the sixth day running after its almost daily actions against the zloty in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, an NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would weaken the zloty would only increase foreign interest in the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Many foreigners only wait for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to knock the zloty down to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," ING Bank's Czyzewski said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected yet more foreign inflows after a pro-market government is formed later in the week. \par \par \uc2  "The bullish zloty sentiment will continue if there are no problems in forming a market-friendly government," Kredyt's Wituszynski said. \par \par \uc2  On the money-market one-day deposits held stable. Overnight rates closed at 22.65/22.70 percent against opening's 22.68/22.78 percent. Tomorrow/next ended at 22.80/23.00 percent against 22.75/22.90. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtae00lzs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
